# Craft A Bot — environment variables
#
# There are none at runtime: the app is local-first with no backend, and the
# user's API key lives in their browser's localStorage (06-LLM-PROVIDERS.md §6),
# never in a file and never in this repo.
#
# What follows is for the headless harness (`npm run craftabot`) and the live
# smoke checkpoints, run by hand on one machine and never in CI
# (10-CODING-STANDARDS.md §5; 112-REAL-ENOUGH-PLAN.md D9). Copy this file to
# `.env` — `.env` is gitignored, and the harness and every `smoke:*` script read it.
# Prefer a separate, spending-capped key for each service, and leave blank what
# you do not use: a blank line is the same as an unset one.
#
# `npm run craftabot -- keys check` says which of these this process holds, by
# id and never by value, and what each one lights. docs/keys.md has the table.
#
# TWO KINDS OF VARIABLE, AND WHY BOTH:
#   CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_<ID>   what the harness reads — runs, recordings, the
#                               benchmark. <ID> is the credential id, upper-cased.
#   the vendor's own names      what a smoke script reads (OPENAI_API_KEY, …).
# A key set in one is not set in the other. Set both for a service you want to
# smoke-test and then record.

# --- OpenAI: the frontier comparison brain (WP166) and `npm run smoke:openai` ---
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_OPENAI=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Other model providers (optional; nothing in the plan needs them) ---
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_ANTHROPIC=
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_GEMINI=

# --- Google Cloud: Model Armor and the Gen AI evaluation service (WP163, WP165) ---
# The token is short-lived: `gcloud auth print-access-token`, the same day you run.
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_GEAP=
GEAP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
GEAP_PROJECT_ID=
GEAP_LOCATION=europe-west2
GEAP_TEMPLATE_ID=cab-armour

# --- Azure AI Content Safety (WP163, WP164) ---
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_AZURE_CONTENT_SAFETY=
AZURE_CONTENT_SAFETY_KEY=
AZURE_CONTENT_SAFETY_ENDPOINT=

# --- Lakera Guard (WP163, WP164) ---
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_LAKERA=
LAKERA_GUARD_KEY=
# LAKERA_GUARD_ENDPOINT=https://api.lakera.ai

# --- AWS Bedrock Guardrails and its automated reasoning (WP163, WP164) ---
# The credential is `accessKeyId:secretAccessKey`; both halves are scrubbed.
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_AWS_BEDROCK=
AWS_BEDROCK_REGION=eu-west-2
AWS_BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_ID=
# AWS_BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_VERSION=DRAFT
AWS_BEDROCK_AR_GUARDRAIL_ID=
# AWS_BEDROCK_AR_GUARDRAIL_VERSION=DRAFT
AWS_BEDROCK_AR_CLAIM=

# --- AWS Verified Permissions: Cedar (WP163) ---
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_AWS_VERIFIED_PERMISSIONS=
AWS_VP_REGION=eu-west-2
AWS_VP_POLICY_STORE_ID=
AWS_VP_DENIED_ACTION=send_email

# --- Other credentials the installed packs declare (optional) ---
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_EVIDENCE_SUPABASE=
CRAFTABOT_CREDENTIAL_TELEMETRY_OTLP_HTTP=

# Editions (WP69, docs/design-day2/59-EDITIONS.md): unset, the build is `full`
# — the whole app under no base. `npm run build:editions` sets this to
# simulator, workshop and playground in turn; it is never read at run time.
# CAB_EDITION=
